Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"GetCoeffSubs", "::", "usage"}], "=", 
  "\"\<GetCoeffSubs[diffeq, g, z, a, teststart, testnlogs, nc] finds the list \
of substitutions of all coefficients in a power-log expansion ansatz solution \
to a differential equation in terms of unconstrained coefficients (to be \
determined by matching conditions).\n\nThe input variables are \n'diffeq': \
the differential equation.\n'g': the function that satisfies the differential \
equation. \n'z': the variable on which 'g' depends.\n'a': a symbol to \
construct the coefficients of the ansatz. \n'teststart': a preliminary test \
lowest power of 'z' in the ansatz (which should be low enough to make sure \
nothing is missed). \n'testnlogs': a preliminary test highest power of the \
log (it should be chosen high enough). \n'nc': the highest power in 'z' in \
the ansatz.\n\nIf in Mathematica several kernels are launched, the underlying \
solver will be executed in parallel mode.\n\nOptions: \\\"Number of coeffs to \
get parameters\\\" sets the number of coefficients used to determine the \
ansatz parameters. Default: 50.\>\""}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.845459607834463*^9, 3.845459638369878*^9}, {
